1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,320
First came the reptilian brain, the

2
00:00:02,320 --> 00:00:05,100
oldest layer, roughly 500 million years

3
00:00:05,100 --> 00:00:07,820
old, handling the functions so basic

4
00:00:07,820 --> 00:00:09,840
they're barely worth listing.

5
00:00:09,840 --> 00:00:13,140
Breathe, eat, fight, flee,

6
00:00:13,140 --> 00:00:14,180
reproduce,

7
00:00:14,180 --> 00:00:16,160
regulate body temperature.

8
00:00:16,160 --> 00:00:16,980
This is the brain

9
00:00:16,980 --> 00:00:18,580
you share with lizards.

10
00:00:18,580 --> 00:00:20,140
It has no feelings.

11
00:00:20,140 --> 00:00:22,100
It has no opinions.

12
00:00:22,100 --> 00:00:23,400
It has reflexes.

13
00:00:23,400 --> 00:00:26,240
And those reflexes kept vertebrates alive

14
00:00:26,240 --> 00:00:29,280
for 300 million years before anything

15
00:00:29,280 --> 00:00:30,980
with fur showed up.

16
00:00:30,980 --> 00:00:32,120
It's still running.

17
00:00:32,120 --> 00:00:33,800
It's running right now.

18
00:00:33,800 --> 00:00:35,020
It's the reason your heart

19
00:00:35,020 --> 00:00:37,160
is beating without your permission.

20
00:00:37,160 --> 00:00:39,400
Then about 200 million years ago, mammals

21
00:00:39,400 --> 00:00:41,560
evolved the limbic system on top of

22
00:00:41,560 --> 00:00:43,860
the reptile brain, like building a nursery

23
00:00:43,860 --> 00:00:46,060
on top of a weapon's depot.

24
00:00:46,060 --> 00:00:48,180
This is your emotional brain.

25
00:00:48,180 --> 00:00:49,540
It's the reason you bond with your

26
00:00:49,540 --> 00:00:51,840
children instead of eating them, a genuine

27
00:00:51,840 --> 00:00:54,080
upgrade over the reptilian model.

28
00:00:54,220 --> 00:00:56,160
It handles fear, pleasure,

29
00:00:56,160 --> 00:00:58,100
memory, and social bonding.

30
00:00:58,100 --> 00:00:59,160
It's the reason you cry at

31
00:00:59,160 --> 00:01:00,880
movies, love your dog, and feel

32
00:01:00,880 --> 00:01:02,540
a physical ache when someone you

33
00:01:02,540 --> 00:01:03,800
care about is hurting.

34
00:01:03,800 --> 00:01:04,540
It is also the

35
00:01:04,540 --> 00:01:06,380
reason you make catastrophically

36
00:01:06,380 --> 00:01:07,840
stupid decisions when you're

37
00:01:07,840 --> 00:01:10,140
angry, aroused, or afraid.

38
00:01:10,140 --> 00:01:11,860
Because the limbic system processes

39
00:01:11,860 --> 00:01:13,780
information faster than the part

40
00:01:13,780 --> 00:01:15,540
of your brain that thinks.

41
00:01:15,540 --> 00:01:17,220
And by the time thinking arrives,

42
00:01:17,220 --> 00:01:19,140
the limbic system has already committed

43
00:01:19,140 --> 00:01:20,880
you to a course of action,

44
00:01:20,880 --> 00:01:23,000
you'll spend the next decade regretting.
